# Screenshot editor flow (thumbnail, history, save, delete). Check in each look.
setup (magick -size 1600x900 xc:white -fill black -pointsize 48 -annotate +100+200 "Invoice total 42.00" -annotate +100+320 "https://example.com/pay" /tmp/t.png || convert -size 1600x900 xc:white -fill black -pointsize 48 -annotate +100+200 "Invoice total 42.00" -annotate +100+320 "https://example.com/pay" /tmp/t.png); cp /tmp/t.png /tmp/t2.png
ipc shotEditor thumbnail /tmp/t.png
wait 1
shot se-thumb
note Thumbnail card about 212x125 at x 1684..1896, y 931..1056, slid in at the bottom right.
ptr move 1790 993 click
wait 1
shot se-editor
note Clicking the thumbnail opens the editor centred. NOTE: click on layer surfaces may not register in the harness.
key -k p
ptr move 500 400 down glide 800 500 200 up
ipc shotEditor thumbnail /tmp/t2.png
wait 1
ptr move 1790 993 click
wait 1
shot se-ask
note Banner "Save changes before opening the new screenshot?" with Keep editing / Discard changes / Save buttons. Discard then reopens the editor on t2 with no marks.
key -k Escape
wait 1
ipc shotEditor close
wait 1
ipc shotEditor edit /tmp/t.png
wait 1
key -k p
ptr move 500 300 down glide 600 350 100 up
ptr move 500 400 down glide 600 450 100 up
ptr move 500 500 down glide 600 550 100 up
key -M ctrl -k z -m ctrl
key -M ctrl -k z -m ctrl
key -M ctrl -M shift -k z -m shift -m ctrl
wait 1
shot se-history
note After 3 marks, Ctrl+Z twice, Ctrl+Shift+Z once: exactly 2 marks are visible, and the Undo/Redo buttons are enabled/disabled to match (Redo enabled, Undo enabled).
key -k a
ptr move 600 700 down glide 1000 700 100 up
key -k Escape
wait 1
key -k Escape
wait 1
ipc shotEditor edit /tmp/t.png
wait 1
shot se-tool-memory
note After closing and reopening the editor the last tool (Arrow) is still selected (highlighted in the top bar); the colour choice (4 Orchid if picked) persists too.
ptr move 500 400 down glide 800 500 100 up
rec se-save 1 key -M ctrl -k s -m ctrl
note Ctrl+S: the editor fades out in about 200 ms and the thumbnail of the saved file slides in; the file on disk has the marks (QML vs Rust timing).
wait 2
ipc shotEditor close
wait 1
ipc shotEditor edit /tmp/t2.png
wait 1
shot se-delete-before
note Editor open on a copy; the trash button is the first action button of the bottom bar.
# MANUAL: Delete + Undo: click the trash in the bottom bar -> toast "Screenshot deleted" with Undo; click Undo -> editor back with the marks; delete again and wait 8 s: the file is in the Trash (needs real clicks on layer surfaces)
ipc shotEditor close
wait 1
shot se-closed
note ipc shotEditor close closes the editor without asking, even with unsaved marks.
